## TL;DR: 3 Mistakes to Avoid Before You Buy

The 3 mistakes every 2 carat asscher cut diamond ring buyer makes:

1. **Shopping natural on a lab budget** — a natural 2ct asscher with VS1 clarity starts at $21,000+ for the stone alone. Lab gives you [IGI 2.01ct D-FL](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28794228?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for [$5,536](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28794228?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Same carat weight. $19,517 gap.
2. **Going below VS1 at 2ct** — at 2ct the asscher's face-up table reaches 7.1mm. Step facets this size amplify every inclusion. VS1 is the hard floor. SI1 or SI2 is a visible problem in normal lighting.
3. **Choosing H color in white metal** — at 2ct, G is the mandatory floor in white gold and platinum. H color reads warm across a 7mm face-up table. It is not subtle.

