## What Is a 2 Carat Asscher Cut Diamond Ring?

A 2 carat asscher cut diamond ring is where the shape becomes a statement. At 2ct, the asscher's face-up table reaches approximately 7.1mm across — large enough that the windmill pattern is visible from across the room.

The 2ct threshold matters for a specific reason: natural asschers cross a rarity cliff at this size. Natural 2ct+ diamonds require clean rough of a size that is genuinely scarce. That scarcity is reflected in every natural 2ct price on the market.

Lab growing eliminates this scarcity entirely. The IGI lab options in this guide are real stones at current certified-market prices — the price difference is not a trade-off in grade, it is a trade-off in origin.

[![Asscher cut diamond ring in yellow gold lifestyle shot on finger with gold bracelets](/images/asscher-cut-diamond-ring-yellow-gold-lifestyle-hands.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/asscher-cut-diamond-rings?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

I'm **Farzana Hasan**, a GIA-Certified Diamond Expert. The 2ct asscher is where lab and natural diverge most dramatically in this entire shape category.

I've evaluated hundreds of asscher cuts across all sizes. The 2ct is the pivot point — below it, some buyers can stretch to natural with careful planning. At 2ct and above, the price gap makes lab the practical default for most budgets.

Knowing which side of that line you are on before you browse saves thousands in wasted time.

Lab delivers [IGI 2.01ct D-FL](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28794228?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for [$5,536](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28794228?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Natural delivers the same carat weight for $21,147–$25,053. Understanding why — and which path is right for you — is what this post covers.

This guide uses certified market inventory — real stone IDs, real setting prices, verified totals. Every number in this post is a stone or setting you can order today. No sample prices, no ballpark ranges.

The same rules apply at 2ct as at every asscher size: VS1 clarity minimum, G color floor, Art Deco settings preferred. What changes is the scale of the consequences when you get those rules wrong.

Full credentials at **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**. For the size below, see the [1.5 Carat Asscher Cut Diamond Ring guide](/1-5-carat-asscher-cut-diamond-ring). Setting styles and metal choices are in the [asscher cut diamond engagement ring guide](/asscher-cut-diamond-engagement-rings).

