</td><td>Excellent — grips all eight corners, stone-forward</td><td>Cleanest look, lowest price, stone dominates</td></tr><tr><td>#4</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-hidden-halo-solitaire-plus-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-192506?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">Petite Hidden Halo YG</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-hidden-halo-solitaire-plus-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-192506?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$1,255</a></td><td>14k Yellow Gold</td><td>Good — hidden halo below table, outline preserved</td><td>Extra sparkle under stone, face-up profile clean</td></tr><tr><td>#5</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-315297?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis RG</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-315297?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$1,190</a></td><td>14k Rose Gold</td><td>Excellent — rose gold softens geometric outline</td><td>Romantic vintage look, same Art Deco detail, warm metal</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** The Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis ranks #1 at 2ct as it does at every asscher size. At 2ct, the 7mm stone fills the Art Deco basket with full presence — the combination looks exactly like what it is: the setting this shape was designed for. The Ten Prong Solitaire is correct if you want the stone to carry the entire visual weight.

[![Asscher cut diamond ring rose gold with channel-set round diamonds on the band](/images/asscher-cut-diamond-ring-rose-gold-channel-set-diamonds.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/asscher-cut-diamond-rings?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

### Solitaire Settings for 2ct

The [Ten Prong Solitaire in white gold at $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the right choice when you want the stone to be the entire ring. At 2ct, a 7mm asscher in a clean white gold solitaire reads clearly from any distance.

The ten prongs sit at the eight corners of the octagonal girdle. At 2ct, corner protection matters — the asscher's corners are vulnerable to chipping at this size, and the ten-prong design covers all eight points correctly.

Yellow gold and rose gold versions are available at the same $860 — [yellow gold here](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-by-james-allen-item-311236?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and [rose gold here](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-311237?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

### Art Deco Settings for 2ct

The [Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis in white gold at $1,190](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315298?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the natural home of the asscher cut at 2ct.

At 2ct, the stone fills the Art Deco basket completely. The pavé shoulders and fleur-de-lis detail frame a 7mm octagonal stone with historical accuracy — the asscher cut, Art Deco setting, and white gold combination is a 1920s design reproduced correctly.

The [rose gold Art Deco version at $1,190](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-315297?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) softens the geometric combination with warm metal. Paired with the [IGI 1.98ct D-FL at $3,848](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29230615?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), the total ring is $5,038.

### Cathedral Settings for 2ct

The [Tapered Cathedral Solitaire in yellow gold at $1,240](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/tapered-cathedral-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-203288?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) elevates the 2ct asscher on an arched rail above the finger.

At 2ct, the elevated profile draws attention to the stone's face-up geometry from the side. The cathedral arch raises the stone 2–3mm above the band — viewing the ring from across a table, the 7mm asscher is fully visible and the windmill pattern is clear.

Yellow gold + cathedral arch + asscher cut is a period-correct combination. All three design elements are from the same 1920s era. The combination is architecturally honest in a way that mixing contemporary settings with this shape rarely achieves.

### Hidden Halo Settings for 2ct

The [Petite Hidden Halo in yellow gold at $1,255](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-hidden-halo-solitaire-plus-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-192506?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) places a ring of small diamonds beneath the table of the asscher, not above it.

The effect at 2ct is sparkle from below — the hidden halo creates a glow at the stone's edge without altering the face-up profile. Looking straight down at a 2ct asscher in a hidden halo, you see the windmill pattern uninterrupted. The halo only appears when the ring tilts.

This setting suits buyers who want the clean face-up profile of a solitaire with extra light return from the side. Total ring with the [IGI 1.98ct D-FL at $3,848](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29230615?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational): $5,103. Total with the [IGI 2.01ct D-FL at $5,536](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28794228?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational): $6,791.

