## How to Buy a 2 Carat Asscher Cut Diamond Ring

Four decisions. In this order. At 2ct, getting them wrong is more expensive than at any other size in this guide.

**Step 1: Set The Total Ring Number first.** At 2ct, the stakes are too high to run this math after. If your total budget is $7,000, your stone budget is $5,760–$6,140 and your setting budget is $860–$1,240.

Calculate before you browse. Falling in love with the [IGI 2.01ct D-FL at $5,536](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28794228?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and then discovering the [Art Deco WG at $1,190](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315298?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) brings the total to $6,726 is not a surprise you want mid-purchase.

**Step 2: Lab or natural — decide before you browse.** At 2ct this decision is a budget boundary, not a preference question. Lab ring: $4,708–$6,776. Natural ring: $22,007–$33,000+.

There is no overlap. If your budget is under $15,000, you are buying lab. Decide that now and browse accordingly.

**Step 3: Apply The Clarity Floor.** VS1 minimum at 2ct. No exceptions. The 7mm face-up table amplifies inclusions more than at any smaller size.

Buying lab? D-FL eliminates this step.

Buying natural? Request the GIA inclusion plot.

Confirm the inclusion position before you finalize. The plot is a visual diagram showing exactly where each inclusion sits — any retailer can share it in 30 seconds.

A VS1 near the girdle is safe. A VS1 under the table is not.

**Step 4: Choose your setting last.** After the stone grade and budget are confirmed. The [Art Deco WG at $1,190](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315298?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the right pairing. The [Ten Prong WG at $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) if you want the stone to carry all the visual weight.

Every buyer who regrets their 2ct ring skipped at least one of these four steps.

The buyer who follows all four ends up with a ring they are still happy with five years later. The buyer who skips Step 1 or Step 2 usually comes back asking what went wrong.

At 2ct, the only mistake that costs more than making the wrong call is making it twice. Get the sequence right the first time.

