## Expert Summary

The 2 carat asscher cut diamond ring is the size where The 2ct Milestone makes lab the correct choice for most buyers. The lab vs natural gap at 2ct is not a modest premium — it is $15,000–$19,000 on the same carat weight.

Lab delivers [IGI 2.01ct D-FL](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28794228?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for [$5,536](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28794228?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Complete rings start at $6,396 and reach $6,776 with the Cathedral YG. Every lab stone in this guide is Flawless — no clarity inspection required.

Natural 2ct asschers begin at [$21,147](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27103714?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for a GIA G-VS2. Complete rings start at $22,007. The natural buyer pays for certified provenance, GIA documentation, and a stone formed in the earth.

That has real value. It is also a $15,000+ premium over the lab alternative at the same carat weight.

All 3 mistakes — wrong budget expectation, below VS1, H color in white metal — lead to the same outcome: you spend more and get a ring that performs below what it should. Apply The Clarity Floor. Calculate The Total Ring Number first.

Understand The 2ct Milestone before you browse.

The rules are simple. VS1 minimum. G color minimum.

Art Deco setting. Calculate The Total Ring Number before you look at a stone. Skip any of these and you pay more for a ring that performs less than it should.

Full asscher cut resources — all sizes, all settings — at the [Asscher Cut Diamond guide](/asscher-cut-diamond).

